; onehot_expansion (QUI-1056): pins the step cost of a single ONEHOTR over
; a 4-column grid row.
;
; ONEHOTR charges equality_expansion_steps(cols) before it expands the
; one-hot constraint (spec/xqvm/METERING.md): for cols=4 that is
; (4 + pairs(4)) * COEFF_WRITE_STEPS = (4 + 6) * 13 = 130 steps, on top of
; each instruction's own BASE_STEPS. This vector asserts both
; implementations charge the same total for that expansion, independent
; of how many map entries the expansion actually writes.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 1
PUSH 4
RESIZE r0

PUSH 0
PUSH 2
ONEHOTR r0
HALT
